From c4d02874982fb0cd1f7c6912e9504b3fae690430 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Chris Allen <cma@bitemyapp.com>
Date: Fri, 6 Nov 2026 01:41:15 -0600
Subject: [PATCH] data_device: Send `wl_data_source.target` when the target
 accepts

A drag target's `wl_data_offer.accept` reached `Source::accepted`, but
`WlDataSource` kept its no-op default, so the source client never got
`wl_data_source.target` and couldn't show whether a drop would be
accepted. Forward the accepted mime type, or none for a rejection, as
Weston and wlroots do.

Found in Aizome, whose drag-and-drop test sees the target's action reach
the source but never its mime type. On smithay 0.7.0 that test, waiting
for `target` as well, times out; with the equivalent one-line change in
0.7.0's `Accept` arm it passes. Smithay has no client harness to test
`wl_data_device` in-tree.

Developed with AI assistance (Claude Code).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 CHANGELOG.md                                | 4 ++++
 src/wayland/selection/data_device/source.rs | 4 ++++
 2 files changed, 8 insertions(+)

diff --git a/CHANGELOG.md b/CHANGELOG.md
index 6c031ccd..78aab34a 100644
--- a/CHANGELOG.md
+++ b/CHANGELOG.md
@@ -292,6 +292,10 @@ additionally drops the buffers cached for copying between a render and a target
 
 ### Bugfixes
 
+Drag and drop now sends `wl_data_source.target` when the target accepts a mime type with
+`wl_data_offer.accept`, or rejects the offer. Previously the source never heard of the target's choice,
+so clients could not give feedback on whether a drop would be accepted.
+
 `LibinputInputBackend` now processes events libinput has queued without making its file descriptor
 readable: the `DeviceAdded` events for devices already present after `Libinput::udev_assign_seat` and
 `Libinput::resume`, and `DeviceRemoved` after `Libinput::suspend`. Previously these waited for the next
diff --git a/src/wayland/selection/data_device/source.rs b/src/wayland/selection/data_device/source.rs
index 09ac7ebd..cdb5b492 100644
--- a/src/wayland/selection/data_device/source.rs
+++ b/src/wayland/selection/data_device/source.rs
@@ -124,6 +124,10 @@ impl Source for WlDataSource {
             .map(|data| data.inner.lock().unwrap().clone())
     }
 
+    fn accepted(&self, mime_type: Option<String>) {
+        self.target(mime_type);
+    }
+
     fn choose_action(&self, action: DndAction) {
         self.action(action.into());
     }
